{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>When you beget children and children's children, and you have grown old</b>. The meaning of this verse is that He makes mention and says: When you beget children and children's children, and because you have grown old in the land and dwell securely, perhaps you will forget the Name — I call witness against you today that you will perish quickly, for you will not last long, once you engage in foreign worship. And this section, although it is a warning, was not stated in the language of \"if,\" for the reason that He is like one prophesying concerning their affairs, and He speaks in language that serves in two ways: as a warning and as a future prediction. He says that they will do so and it will befall them accordingly, yet He does not decree it upon them. And because of this, our Sages said (Gittin 88a) that He alluded to the exile of the First Temple through the word <b>ונושנתם</b> by way of gematria, and there was a tradition in their hands that there is in this section a hint to the time of the exile, and when it came upon them they understood it with insight." "And He said, <b>and you make a carved image, the form of anything</b>, and did not say <b>and you worship it</b> or <b>and you bow down to it</b>, but rather said <b>and you deal corruptly</b>, for the carved image here is the form of anything, and because of the corruption He will banish them, as I explained above."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:31.523808053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}